# Review: AssistantPlugin

The core chat loop is solid and broadly tested: chat creation with default skill bindings, streaming,
automatic naming after the first prompt, `BindChatContext`, skill binding from the registry and slash
commands, trace capture, and the struggle-report hook (`AnalyzeTurn`) all have node tests. The spec's
data model has drifted. `Chat` has no `messages` array: it holds a ref to an ECHO `Feed` of
`@dxos/types` `Message` objects, which carry `sender` and content `blocks` rather than `role` and
`content`. `ModelProvider` is an open DXN, not a three-value literal. `ToggleTracePanelDebug` is now
`SetTracePanelDebug`, which takes a required `state` and no longer flips. `CreateChat` returns an
unfiled chat and has no `db` or `addToSpace` input.

The clearest gap is `OnCreateSpace`. The assistant contributes no `SpaceCapabilities.OnCreateSpace`, so
F-6.2 is missing. `EnsureCompanionChat`, `RunPromptInNewChat`, the code-mode turn producer and the
resolver fallback chain are implemented but no test drives them. No scenario except T-1 (partly) has
automation.

Of 55 items: 17 done, 17 untested, 4 partial, 7 diverged, 10 missing.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

